master|Master Flag|||0|1|
UnUsedParameter|UnUsedParameter|||||
FadcConstraint|Fadc Constraint|||8000000|26000000|
Mode|Mode|ADCsgroup||||Multi ADC mode selection: Configures the ADC to operate in independent or multi mode
DMAAccessModeView|DMA Access Mode|ADCsgroup||||
DMAAccessMode|DMA Access Mode|ADCsgroup||||
TwoSamplingDelay|Delay between 2 sampling phases|ADCsgroup||||Delay between 2 sampling phases
ClockPrescaler|Clock Prescaler|ADCsgroup||||frequency of the clock to the ADC. The clock is common for all the ADCs.
Resolution|Resolution|ADCGroup||||Resolution of the ADC conversion
DataAlign|Data Alignment3|ADCGroup||||The alignment mode is available only on for Regular conversion. Injected conversion working with oversampling: the data are always provided right-aligned.
ScanConvMode|Scan Conversion Mode|ADCGroup||||Enable or Disable the Scan Conversion Mode
ContinuousConvMode|Continuous Conversion Mode|ADCGroup||||Enable or Disable the Continuous Conversion Mode
DiscontinuousConvMode|Discontinuous Conversion Mode|ADCGroup||||Discontinuous Conversion Mode
NbrOfDiscConversion|Number Of Discontinuous Conversions|ADCgroup||1|8|
DMAContinuousRequests|DMA Continuous Requests|ADCgroup||||This parameter is used only when a DMA Request is configured. Else it is not relevant. When the DMA Request for this ADC instance this parameter specifies whether the DMA requests are performed in one shot mode (DMA transfer stops when number of conversions is reached) or are performed in continuous mode (DMA transfer unlimited, whatever number of conversions). Note: In continuous mode, DMA must be configured in circular mode. Otherwise an overrun will be triggered when DMA buffer maximum pointer is reached.
DMAContinuousRequestsForConfigFile|DMA Continuous Requests|ADCGroup||||Enable/Disable DMA Continuous Requests
EOCSelection|End Of Conversion Selection|ADCGroup||||Regular channel end of conversion selection
Overrun|Overrun behaviour|ADCGroup||||Select the behaviour in case of overrun
DFSDMConfig|DFSDM transfer of ADC conversion|ADCGroup||||Specify whether ADC conversion data is sent directly to DFSDM
LowPowerAutoWait|Low Power Auto Wait|ADCGroup||||Specifies the usage of Low Power Auto Wait Mode: new conversion start only when the previous conversion (for regular group) or previous sequence (for injected group) has been treated by user software.
EnableRegularConversion|Enable Regular Conversions|ADC_Regular_ConversionMode||||Enable/Disable Regular Conversion
OversamplingMode|Enable Regular Oversampling|ADC_Regular_ConversionMode||||Enable/Disable Regular Oversampling
